5. A common mistake: max() (or first()) as the 'favorite'
========================================================================
+--------+--------+
|customer|favorite|
+--------+--------+
|   alice|     mug|
|     bob|     tea|
|   carol|  teapot|
+--------+--------+

alice bought coffee 3 times and a mug once, yet her coupon is for
MUGS: max() of a string is the alphabetically last value ('mug' >
'coffee'). bob's 'tea' is right only by luck. F.first() is no better:
whichever row comes first, non-deterministic after a shuffle.
'Most often' is a count: use mode(), or count per product (section 3).
